# A SOURCE FILE WITH A NUL IN IT IS STILL A SOURCE FILE.
#
# connectors/lib/linkedinRows.mjs carries a literal NUL — the separator in
# sha8's `parts.join('\0')` — so git classified the whole file as binary and
# rendered every diff of it as "Binary files differ". A change to its date
# parser went through a review round invisible to the reviewer, to GitHub and
# to `git diff`, which is the kind of gap nobody notices until it has already
# cost something.
#
# Declared for the tree rather than fixed at the call site: the separator is
# load-bearing (a NUL cannot appear in the fields being joined, which is why it
# was chosen), and the next file to embed one should not have to rediscover
# this.
*.mjs diff
*.js diff
*.swift diff
